MID_SE_Led_Tal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_001: Ah, Lady Leda. Keeping busy, I see. That's...\nObsidian, isn't it?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_002: Yes—I'm tuning it. I try to do this once a day, when I\nhave time.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_003: How attentive. I didn't realize you put so much care\ninto your instrument.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_004: Are you trying to insult me? To a musician, tuning\none's instrument is like breathing.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_005: The fact you'd suggest otherwise betrays\nyour ignorance.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_006: Mhm... That'll do.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_007: Seems it's the beauty of the instrument AND\nthe musician that truly make a melody.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_008: Again with the facile comments. You don't know\nthe first thing about good musicianship, do you?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_009: I admit, Obsidian in my hands wouldn't sound nearly\nas sweet as in yours. But we merchants know our art.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_010: I even know my way around a vihuela myself,\nbelieve it or not.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_011: Oh. So, you learned the rudiments from some girl\nyou were seeing? Or just used it to pick up women?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_012: Nope. In fact, it was a man that taught me the\nstrings. And I practiced purely for friendship.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_013: Perhaps it'd be faster to show you. Wait right here.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_014: That's...Maria's vihuela!
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_015: She called it Moonstone. A lucky find, indeed.\nNow, listen close...
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_016: ♪
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_017: Here, mind if I borrow that a sec?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_018: Hey, give that back! You won't be able to play\nit anyway.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_019: ♪
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_020: You can actually play it.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_021: And your musicianship is better than most bards'.\nI never would have expected that.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_022: I'll try to take your surprise as a compliment.\nThat being said... Here.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_023: Huh? Why would you give me Moonstone?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_024: I want you to have it, of course. As skilled as I may\nbe with it, it only tends to bring out the gloom in me.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_025: They say you're the reincarnation of the Virtuosa\nof Heaven and Earth. I can't think of a better owner.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_026: "Virtuosa Reincarnate," yeah... Fine. I'll put it to\nbetter use than you would anyway.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_027: Happy to hear it! But you've gotta admit, I wasn't\nhalf bad, was I?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_028: Rude as ever, I see... Here.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_029: I'm rude? You're the one who took my vihuela and\nplayed it without asking!
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_030: But at least you see it now, right? I'm pretty good,\naren't I?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_031: Well—fine, yes. I admit that you're not completely\nwithout skill.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_032: Hahaha. I'll take what I can get and quit while\nI'm ahead! I'll be seeing you.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_033: What was that about? Was it that important to him\nto show off?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_034: Either way, it doesn't make sense. This vihuela has\na curse on it—it chooses its owner.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_B_035: If you're not chosen, you can't even get it to play\na tune... So, how did he do it? And so well?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_001: Mmm... You know, you almost remind me of the\nbard Cohen.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_002: Because I have Obsidian, you mean? And, well—\nI am his descendant.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_003: Nah, it's more than just his bloodline—it's the way\nyou carry yourself that strikes me.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_004: I knew him, you know. Hmhmhmm. Couldn't forget\nthe man if I tried.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_005: You met Cohen while he was still alive?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_006: Is that how you could play a cursed vihuela?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_007: Couldn't say. It was nearly five hundred years ago,\nafter all.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_008: When my father died, my family fell into ruin.\nAnd I couldn't stand to stick around for all that.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_009: I left everything behind and traveled Dagda all by\nmy lonesome, you see.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_010: That's when Cohen and I first met. Feels like ages\nago now.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_011: Ahh. Sure. Still doesn't explain how some salesman\nlearns to play the way you do.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_012: I was still just a wild kid. And he'd just left the\ntemple, if I'm not mistaken.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_013: Cohen was this sensitive poet, and I was...well.\nLet's just say we couldn't have had less in common.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_014: But we both had divine blood in our veins—both\ncraved adventure! So strangely enough, we got on.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_015: It was short, but some of the best times of my life.\nSomewhere in there, he taught me the vihuela.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_016: My skill with it is only thanks to him. So if I'm able\nto strum cursed strings, maybe I owe him that too.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_017: That would explain it.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_018: I always saw the legend he would be. I see the same\nthing when I look at you, Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_019: Oh! You think I'll become a legend like him. Based\non my musical talents, hm?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_020: Or could it be that you think I'll meet a tragic end,\nlike he did? Because I'm sick of hearing about that.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_021: No, no. I think you misunderstand.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_022: Cohen was an expert musician, sure. But he was also\nkind and vulnerable. And even above all that...
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_023: He was a man determined to cut his own path\nthrough the world. That's who my friend was to me.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_024: With your skill with the strings, and that fire in your\neyes, I get the same feeling now.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_025: The truth is...I'm nothing like him. I don't have any\npassion for song, or playing the vihuela.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_026: To me, music is...a tool. It's a way to get by,\nand deceive people, and fight.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_027: Hey, now! I'm pouring my heart out to you...
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_028: Here I am, sharing tender memories of a bygone era.\nYou're gonna make your ancestor cry, Lady Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_029: Well. I suppose you're right I share Cohen's skill.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_030: Oh?
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_031: And the determination to forge my own path.\nSo we're not entirely dissimilar.
MID_SE_Led_Tal_A_032: Hmhmhm. Damn. I guess not everyone knows how\nto take a compliment.